{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 14, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b", "content": "**My Unforgettable Journey to Japan**\n\nStepping off the plane in Tokyo, I was immediately greeted by a symphony of neon lights and the electric hum of a city that never sleeps. My trip to Japan was a perfect blend of ancient tradition and futuristic innovation.\n\nThe journey began in the bustling Shibuya Crossing, where thousands of people surged across the intersection in perfect synchronization. Yet, just a short train ride away, the atmosphere shifted entirely. In the serene temples of Kyoto, the air was thick with incense and silence. I watched monks sweep the gravel gardens at Kinkaku-ji, the Golden Pavilion, reflecting perfectly in the still pond. The contrast between the chaotic energy of Tokyo and the meditative peace of Kyoto was the highlight of the trip.\n\nFood was another adventure entirely. From steaming bowls of ramen in narrow alleyways to delicate, artistic kaiseki dinners, every meal told a story. I still dream about the melt-in-your-mouth sushi at a tiny counter in Osaka, where the chef's years of experience were evident in every slice.\n\nThe Shinkansen, or bullet train, whisked me between cities at breathtaking speeds, offering views of Mount Fuji on a rare clear day. Its snow-capped peak stood as a silent guardian over the landscape, a moment of pure awe.\n\nJapan taught me to appreciate the beauty in small details, from the precision of a tea ceremony to the kindness of strangers who helped me navigate the subway. It was a trip that engaged all the senses and left a lasting mark on my heart. I can already feel the pull to return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.29092026}, {"token": "My", "logprob": -4.8010917}, {"token": " Un", "logprob": -0.008537092}, {"token": "forgettable", "logprob": -5.960466e-07}, {"token": " Journey", "logprob": -0.0046558115}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -1.3672869}, {"token": " Japan", "log